# `src/assets.js` and `lib/` are generated output:
#
#   node scripts/embed-assets.mjs   src/assets.js   <- assets/*.jpg + assets/lightness.json
#   node scripts/build.mjs          lib/            <- src/
#
# Both are deterministic functions of the committed sources, and both used to be
# ignored because `lib/client.js` is a single 3.8 MB file carrying every artwork as
# base64, so committing it grows the history on every art edit.
#
# They are committed anyway, because this package is installed as a git dependency
# (`github:jeweis/dsh-skin-lab`) and `package.json` points `main` and
# `exports["./client"]` straight at `lib/`. A git dependency is consumed as a clone:
# nothing rebuilds it, and since pnpm 10.26 a git-hosted dependency is blocked from
# running `prepare` unless it is allowlisted (pnpm/pnpm#10288), so a `prepare` script
# is not a way out either. Ignoring the build output therefore ships a package whose
# entry point does not exist.
#
# Cost of committing: history growth on art edits. Cost of not committing: the plugin
# cannot be installed at all.
#
# `scripts/prepare-assets.py` is NOT needed for any of that: it only turns the original
# PNG masters (which are not in this repo) into assets/*.jpg, and those are committed.

# Python bytecode from scripts/prepare-assets.py and scripts/analyze-render.py
__pycache__/
node_modules/
*.log
.DS_Store
